From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:11:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] EDAT reader: the cache check reads the size with 64 bits

Symptom: on Windows every start of the game took as long as the install's data step (36 s under Wine, longer on a
hard disk) before the first movie: the 3 GB data archive was decrypted again each time (found on the maintainer's
Windows PC 2026-11-16, reproduced with the Windows build under Wine: a second start printed "[edat] decrypted" again).

Cause: patch 4014's cache check compared the cached file's size from stat() with the header's. On MinGW stat's
st_size is a 32-bit _off_t, so a 3 GB file never matched and the cache was always taken as stale (ppu_fs.cpp already
uses _stat64 for the same reason).

Fix: edat_file_size(), _stat64 on Windows and stat elsewhere, for the cache check. Written here. Test:
tools/tests/test_edat_seek.c (the size of a sparse 2.5 GiB file), on Linux and in tools/wine-host-tests.sh.
Upstream candidate together with 4014.
---
 libs/filesystem/edat.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/filesystem/edat.c b/libs/filesystem/edat.c
index 26d375c..459c00d 100644
--- a/libs/filesystem/edat.c
+++ b/libs/filesystem/edat.c
@@ -408,6 +408,19 @@ int edat_selftest(void)
  * -----------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /* A 64-bit seek. fseek takes a long, which is 32 bits on Windows: past 2 GiB
  * (a 3 GB data archive) it fails, and every later block read with it. */
+/* A file's size as 64 bits; -1 when it is not there. stat's st_size is a 32-bit _off_t on MinGW: a 3 GB cache never
+ * matched its header's size, so every start decrypted the archive again. */
+static int64_t edat_file_size(const char* path)
+{
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    struct _stat64 st;
+    return _stat64(path, &st) == 0 ? (int64_t)st.st_size : -1;
+#else
+    struct stat st;
+    return stat(path, &st) == 0 ? (int64_t)st.st_size : -1;
+#endif
+}
+
 static int edat_seek(FILE* f, uint64_t off)
 {
 #ifdef _WIN32
@@ -760,8 +773,7 @@ static void edat_cache_key(const uint8_t hdr[0x90], uint8_t key[0x38])
 
 static int edat_cache_valid(const char* dec, const char* keyf, const uint8_t key[0x38], uint64_t size)
 {
-    struct stat ds;
-    if (stat(dec, &ds) != 0 || (uint64_t)ds.st_size != size) return 0;
+    if (edat_file_size(dec) != (int64_t)size) return 0;
     FILE* k = fopen(keyf, "rb");
     if (!k) return 0;
     uint8_t got[0x38];
